 Cloud routines and unattended sessions follow `docs/agents/OPERATING-MODEL.md`: role files in `.claude/agents/`, routine prompts in `docs/agents/routines/`, autonomy levels L1/L2/L3, and the human-only `approved` / `l3-go` labels. `.claude/hooks/agent-guard.mjs` enforces the hard limits when `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true` or `PINHUNT_AGENT=1`. It is inert in local sessions. Tests: `pnpm test` (vitest + supertest in `api-server`, jest-expo in the app, `node --test` suites). UI screenshots: `pnpm --filter @workspace/pinhunt run screenshots` (Expo web export in demo mock mode via `lib/demoMode.ts`; demo mode can only activate when Supabase is not configured).
 
+### Model routing
+
+Every session and subagent follows `docs/agents/MODEL-ROUTING.md`: **Opus** for architecture, complex debugging, security, critical infrastructure and high-risk changes; **Sonnet** for standard features, UX, API integrations, code review and moderate tasks; **Haiku** for catalogue research, data validation, straightforward fixes, docs, routine tests and repetitive work. Use the cheapest tier that will reliably succeed and escalate one tier on failure. Always pass an explicit `model` when launching an `Agent`; `.claude/settings.json` sets `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=sonnet` so unlabelled subagents never inherit Opus, and each `.claude/agents/*.md` role pins its own model.
